# Changelog content policy

This file is the only editorial policy. Skills, hooks, and human docs point here. Do not copy a second policy.

Audience is customers, operators (org owners and admins), and external integrators. Not CI, agents, or repo-only tooling.

## Include

Write a `CHANGELOG.md` bullet only when the change is one of these:

- New user-visible capability
- Bug fix users or operators can notice
- Security fix
- Breaking or notable workflow change
- Removal or deprecation users will notice
- Performance users can feel

## Omit or batch

Do not write implementation tours. Do not cut a versioned release for these alone:

- Routine Dependabot or dependency patches with no user-visible effect. Add a short `[Unreleased]` note when preview CI requires one for lockfile or `package.json` diffs. At `/release`, batch those notes into one dependency bullet or drop them if nothing user-facing shipped.
- Internal refactors with no behavior change
- CI jobs, test infra, agent scripts, and Cursor rules or skills, unless operator-facing release behavior changed
- File paths, migration filenames, test counts, LOC, job names, "how we built it"

## Bullet shape

Prefer:

    - **Short bold title** — One sentence of user or operator impact. (#issue or #PR)

One bullet is one outcome. Usually two lines or fewer. Issue or PR numbers are encouraged.

## Train and SemVer

- PRs into `preview`: accumulate under `## [Unreleased]` only. Never bump the app version in `package.json`.
- `/release` (`preview` → `main`): one SemVer decision for the whole batch. Empty `[Unreleased]` into one `## [X.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD`. Rewrite bullets into the short style above. Do not move verbose prose as-is.
- Patch: fixes, security without product-shape change, batched dependencies, small UX corrections. Do not cut a patch solely for one dependency bump.
- Minor: new customer-visible capability or meaningful workflow expansion.
- Major: only when the user explicitly requests a breaking customer-visible change.

Use Keep a Changelog categories only when non-empty: Added, Changed, Deprecated, Removed, Fixed, Security.

Do not rewrite historical sections. Entries through the latest released version stay as written.
